Answer: Based on the provided search result, there is no evidence that Vice President Yemi Osinbajo or his office made any public statement prior to September 2020 detailing his personal role in detecting the P&ID fraud. The article describes his documented involvement and correspondence with other officials, including a handwritten note in June 2018 calling the transaction "a fraud on the nation," but it frames these as internal governmental actions that were later highlighted in a UK court ruling rather than proactive public disclosures.

